# Key names only. Never commit real values — see .claude/rules/security.md.
# Copy to .env and fill in locally; on Fly these are set with `fly secrets set`.

# The unguessable URL path segment that gates every real route. This is the
# entire auth model, so a short one is the only way it fails. Minimum 32
# characters, enforced at boot — the process refuses to start below that.
#
#   generate with: openssl rand -hex 24
MCP_SECRET_PATH=
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Fine-grained GitHub personal access token for the two repos this server
# touches — Portfolio-new and workshop. It needs THREE grants, not one:
#
#   Portfolio-new   Contents: read and write
#   Portfolio-new   Pull requests: read and write
#   workshop        Contents: read and write
#
# Contents and Pull requests are SEPARATE permissions. Contents alone lets the
# server commit and branch, then fails at publish time with
# 403 "Resource not accessible by personal access token". The health check
# tests reachability, not scopes, so a half-granted token looks healthy right
# up until someone publishes. See ADR-006.
#
# Contents: write on Portfolio-new also permits committing straight to main.
# Nothing in the code will try, but the guarantee is the ruleset on that
# branch requiring a pull request — not this token. Do not remove it.
#
# Must start with `github_pat_`; a classic `ghp_` token is rejected at boot,
# because GitHub answers 404 for a repo a token cannot see and a wrong token
# would otherwise look like a missing file.
#
#   create at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Port to listen on. Optional; defaults to 3000. Fly sets this from fly.toml.
PORT=
